# Committed on purpose, and it is the SEARCH side only - `graft/` itself stays
# gitignored and is never committed. `graft build` writes this file. ripgrep
# reads .ignore BEFORE .gitignore, so `!graft/` re-admits the index to SEARCH
# while `graft/` in .gitignore keeps it out of COMMITS.
#
# VERIFIED 18 Aug 2026, and the first two attempts proved nothing: rg also reads
# the PARENT clone's .ignore, so deleting only this one changed no result. With
# BOTH removed a root-level `rg` found 0 graft cards; restoring this one alone
# brought them back. That is the test - one file at a time is confounded.
!graft/
graft/.cache/
graft/.graph/

# Agent worktrees build their own 16 MB index at .claude/worktrees/<name>/graft/,
# and `!graft/` above is unanchored, so on its own it would re-admit those too -
# giving duplicate hits that point at that worktree's OWN OLDER SOURCE. Same
# trap vite.config.js records for vitest's `include`, where `**/` collected
# every test twice and the copies ran against stale code.
#
# ⚠️ MEASURED, IT IS NOT BITING TODAY, AND THIS LINE IS STILL WORTH KEEPING.
# Two other things already hide it: rg skips dot-directories unless `--hidden`,
# and rg reads `.git/info/exclude`, which carries `.claude/worktrees/` on this
# machine. Both are weaker than they look - the first stops applying the moment
# somebody passes `--hidden`, and the second is LOCAL and never committed, so it
# does not exist on a fresh clone. This line is the only copy that travels.
.claude/worktrees/
